   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 719 of the laws of 1980 amending the local finance law\nrelating to the period of probable usefulness of certain judgments,\ncompromised claims or settled claims, in relation to extending the provisions\nof such chapter",
    "basePrintNo": "S7080",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7080-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 719 of 1980",
    "lawSection": "Local Finance",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7080\n\nSPONSOR: MARTINEZ\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 719 of the laws of 1980 amending the local\nfinance law relating to the period of probable usefulness of certain\njudgments, compromised claims or settled claims, in relation to extend-\ning the provisions of such chapter\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe bill extends authority from June 15, 2023 to June 15, 2028, for\nmunicipalities to finance judgments related to certain tax proceedings\nincluding certiorari and small claims assessment review.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends chapter 719 of the laws of 1980 and chapter 122 of the\nlaws of 2018 to extend provisions of subdivision 33-a of section 11.00\nof the local finance law for an additional five years.\n\nSection 2 sets an immediate effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nAllowing municipalities to spread the cost of certain judgments over\nseveral years will result in the judgments having less of an impact on\nthe current fiscal year's budget. This authorization should be extended\nfor an additional five years, thereby continuing flexibility provided to\nmunicipalities to pay certain judgments, and providing the legislature\nan opportunity to review the law.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter 87 of the laws of 2018\n\nChapter 77 of the laws of 2013\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act will take effect immediately.\n",
